<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Wy'east Trail</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:131-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.305235" lon="-121.779494"><ele>1104.8</ele><name>Glacier View Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:glacier-view-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 133; book_elev_ft: 3700; quote: The Wy'east Trail starts at the Glacier View Sno-Park</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.304000" lon="-121.772500"><ele>1125.1</ele><name>Powerline north of Highway 26</name><desc>source: placed north of the highway between the sno-park and Ski Bowl; confidence: low; pdf_page: 134; quote: From west to east the classic route begins with the Glacier View Loop, then follows an unmarked powerline route on the north side of Highway 26 to the Ski Bowl.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.302249" lon="-121.769557"><ele>1129.7</ele><name>Ski Bowl Sno-Park (Summit Trail west end)</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:ski-bowl-sno-park; west end of USFS Summit trail 691; confidence: high; pdf_page: 134; quote: From west to east the classic route begins with the Glacier View Loop, then follows an unmarked powerline route on the north side of Highway 26 to the Ski Bowl.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.301320" lon="-121.746000"><ele>1205.0</ele><name>Summit Trail east end (Barlow Trail start)</name><desc>source: USFS 691 east end, by Summit Sno-Park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 134; quote: From there, ski the Summit Trail, Barlow Trail, Summit Meadows Trail, and Red Top Meadows Trail to Trillium Lake Sno-Park.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.295100" lon="-121.738300"><ele>1149.0</ele><name>Barlow Trail south end</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-601A south end, start of SNO-2656D Trillium-Barlow Nordic; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 134; quote: From there, ski the Summit Trail, Barlow Trail, Summit Meadows Trail, and Red Top Meadows Trail to Trillium Lake Sno-Park.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.286110" lon="-121.737480"><ele>1117.0</ele><name>Summit Meadows, north side</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-2656D south end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 134; quote: From there, ski the Summit Trail, Barlow Trail, Summit Meadows Trail, and Red Top Meadows Trail to Trillium Lake Sno-Park.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.283730" lon="-121.737590"><ele>1114.4</ele><name>Summit Meadows, south side</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-2656C piece north end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 134; quote: From there, ski the Summit Trail, Barlow Trail, Summit Meadows Trail, and Red Top Meadows Trail to Trillium Lake Sno-Park.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.280630" lon="-121.732610"><ele>1104.1</ele><name>Red Top Meadows Trail west end</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-689 west end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 134; quote: From there, ski the Summit Trail, Barlow Trail, Summit Meadows Trail, and Red Top Meadows Trail to Trillium Lake Sno-Park.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.284400" lon="-121.727580"><ele>1152.2</ele><name>Red Top Meadows Trail east end</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-689 east end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 134; quote: From there, ski the Summit Trail, Barlow Trail, Summit Meadows Trail, and Red Top Meadows Trail to Trillium Lake Sno-Park.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.285259" lon="-121.727970"><ele>1156.8</ele><name>Trillium Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:trillium-lake-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 134; quote: From there, ski the Summit Trail, Barlow Trail, Summit Meadows Trail, and Red Top Meadows Trail to Trillium Lake Sno-Park.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.287270" lon="-121.728448"><ele>1169.1</ele><name>Snow Bunny Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:snow-bunny-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 134; quote: Cross the highway and ski through unmarked forest to the Salmon River area, where a segment of the old pioneer Barlow Road (the Pioneer North Loop) continues to the Pioneer Woman's Grave.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.286200" lon="-121.718000"><ele>1111.5</ele><name>Forest north of Highway 26</name><desc>source: placed north of the highway, west of the 26/35 junction; confidence: low; pdf_page: 134; quote: Cross the highway and ski through unmarked forest to the Salmon River area, where a segment of the old pioneer Barlow Road (the Pioneer North Loop) continues to the Pioneer Woman's Grave.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.283900" lon="-121.706900"><ele>1122.4</ele><name>Pioneer North Loop start (Road 3531 at Highway 35)</name><desc>source: OSM Forest Road 3531 west end (way 5041285), by Pioneer Woman Sno-Park; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 134; quote: Cross the highway and ski through unmarked forest to the Salmon River area, where a segment of the old pioneer Barlow Road (the Pioneer North Loop) continues to the Pioneer Woman's Grave.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.281900" lon="-121.698500"><ele>1132.4</ele><name>Pioneer Woman's Grave</name><desc>source: west end of OSM Pioneer Woman's Grave Trail #485, where Road 3531 passes; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 134; quote: Cross the highway and ski through unmarked forest to the Salmon River area, where a segment of the old pioneer Barlow Road (the Pioneer North Loop) continues to the Pioneer Woman's Grave.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.282436" lon="-121.685554"><ele>1267.4</ele><name>Barlow Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:barlow-pass-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 134; book_elev_ft: 4157; quote: From there, ski the Buzzard Point Trail (or Barlow Road Trail) to Barlow Pass. Continue on the Mineral Jane Trail over Barlow Saddle to White River.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.281800" lon="-121.677000"><ele>1251.6</ele><name>Mineral Jane Trail (mapped piece, west end)</name><desc>source: OSM Mineral Jane Ski Trail way 548899767 west end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 177; quote: descend the Devils Half Acre Trail 250 yards, then turn left onto the Mineral Jane Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.281800" lon="-121.675300"><ele>1256.4</ele><name>Mineral Jane Trail (mapped piece, east end)</name><desc>source: OSM Mineral Jane Ski Trail way 548899767 east end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 177; quote: descend the Devils Half Acre Trail 250 yards, then turn left onto the Mineral Jane Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.289500" lon="-121.668000"><ele>1194.5</ele><name>Barlow Saddle</name><desc>source: placed east of Highway 35 at its low point (DEM about 3,950 ft); confidence: low; pdf_page: 134; quote: From there, ski the Buzzard Point Trail (or Barlow Road Trail) to Barlow Pass. Continue on the Mineral Jane Trail over Barlow Saddle to White River.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.303000" lon="-121.672800"><ele>1297.7</ele><name>Mineral Jane north end</name><desc>source: placed across the highway from White River West Sno-Park; confidence: low; pdf_page: 180; quote: The north end of the trail starts across the highway from White River West Sno-Park</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.304539" lon="-121.669446"><ele>1289.7</ele><name>White River East Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:white-river-east-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 134; quote: Cross the highway bridge to White River East Sno-Park and ski Mineral Jane Trail East to Bennett Pass.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.304600" lon="-121.663100"><ele>1258.3</ele><name>Leave Road 48</name><desc>source: OSM Wamic Road node where it bends south; confidence: low; pdf_page: 181; quote: follows Road 48, then logging roads, and finally a forest ski trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.308000" lon="-121.652000"><ele>1365.5</ele><name>Mineral Jane East midway</name><desc>source: placed between Road 48 and Bennett Pass; confidence: low; pdf_page: 181; quote: climbing 575 feet to Bennett Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.310224" lon="-121.641836"><ele>1426.3</ele><name>Bennett Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:bennett-pass-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 134; book_elev_ft: 4670; quote: Cross the highway bridge to White River East Sno-Park and ski Mineral Jane Trail East to Bennett Pass.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.302190" lon="-121.602840"><ele>1286.8</ele><name>Upper Junction of Pocket Creek</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-679A Meadows Creek south end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 203; quote: perhaps the East Fork and Meadows Creek Trails are the most scenic and interesting.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.316500" lon="-121.596300"><ele>1206.5</ele><name>Meadows Creek Tie junction</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-679 west end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 203; quote: Meadows Creek Tie Trail ... joins the Meadows Creek Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.325000" lon="-121.580900"><ele>1146.0</ele><name>Tie meets Pocket Creek Trail</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-679 east end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 203; quote: takes off 0.4 mile from Pocket Creek Sno-Park</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.329021" lon="-121.586759"><ele>1162.9</ele><name>Pocket Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:pocket-creek-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 133; book_elev_ft: 3800; quote: ends at the Pocket Creek trailhead</desc></wpt>
